# UI design (shelf tag)

Ink on paper with one price-tag yellow. Tokens live in `apps/web/app/app.css`; use them, never Tailwind palette colors or hex literals.

## Color

- `background`/`card`/`popover`: paper. `foreground`/`primary`: ink. `muted-foreground`: secondary text.
- `success` = money in, `warning` = near a limit (including 90%+), `destructive` = over a limit or delete. A negative net or balance stays ink; its "−" sign carries the meaning. Status messages (offline, saved, imported) use foreground or `muted-foreground`.
- `tag` (yellow) is a fill only, always with `text-tag-foreground`. It appears in three places: the nav wordmark, the dashboard hero price tag, and today's marker. Don't add more.
- Grocery tag colors: stored names map to `--tag-*` dots via `components/groceries/constants.ts`.

## Type

- `type-display` (Archivo, condensed, 800): page titles (`text-title-sm md:text-title`), hero figures, the wordmark. Nothing else.
- Body (Atkinson Hyperlegible Next): 400 and 600. Section headings use `text-heading font-semibold`; subgroup labels inside a section (Shared/Personal, a date within a list) and popover titles use `text-sm font-semibold text-muted-foreground`.
- Figures: every amount in rows and forms uses `font-mono font-medium` (Atkinson Hyperlegible Mono). Ledger dates and invite codes use `font-mono` at regular weight.
- Hero amounts use `PriceTag`, never a bare big number.
- No uppercase letter-spaced labels, no text below 12px.

## Shape and motion

- `rounded-md` (6px) for buttons, inputs, and selects; `rounded-xl` (10px) for panels and dialogs. Checkboxes, color swatches, and tag dots stay square (`rounded-sm` or smaller). 1px `border-border` rules.
- Shadows only on dialogs, popovers, menus, and toasts (`shadow-lg`). No blur, gradients, or colored shadows.
- No load, stagger, hover-lift, press-scale, or pulse animation. Overlays may use `animate-appear`.
- Icons only on controls (add, edit, delete, nav, disclosure). No icons in tinted tiles, no emoji.

## App icon

- The app icon is the nav wordmark: the yellow "amigo" label (Archivo, 75% width, 800) centered on paper. `public/icon.svg` holds the outlined glyphs and is the source for the icon PNGs. Tile corners are 18.75% (6px at 32px). `icon-maskable-512.png` shrinks the label to fit Android's circle crop; it and `apple-touch-icon.png` are opaque with square corners.
- Below 48px the label can't be read, so `favicon.svg` is the wordmark's "a" in ink on a yellow tile, and `badge-96.png` is the "a" alone in white for Android notification badges.

## Copy

- Sentence case everywhere. No taglines under page titles.
- Buttons name the action: "Save loan", "Add budget" — not "Submit" or "Confirm".
- Empty states say what's missing here and offer the action. Errors say what failed and what to do; never "Something went wrong" alone, never "Oops".
- "…" (one character) for in-progress labels; U+2212 "−" for negative amounts.

`apps/web/app/design-guard.test.ts` fails the unit suite on the banned patterns above, including palette classes and hex colors in classes.
